# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (set on this machine) converts files to
# CRLF on checkout while Prettier defaults to `endOfLine: "lf"` - so every
# checked-out file reports `Delete ␍` on every line. The repo ended up mixed:
# 35 files CRLF, 141 LF.
#
# LF is the right canonical form here: this app is built and run in Linux
# containers, where CRLF in a shell script or entrypoint is a runtime failure.
# .gitattributes also travels with the repo, so it fixes every clone regardless
# of each developer's local git config - which `core.autocrlf` does not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
